From fb48dc08bc2ab2ee2390f472ca295ac8fa7e8247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: the native pages' CGIs, an apply is a POST, one page
 table, Wallguard and Encrypted DNS

web.c: reaper_wallguard.cgi and reaper_encdns.cgi (status, saves, lists, Why?,
Unbreak, pause, live view, Apple profile) behind the existing gate; the
native pages' reads with secrets masked (VPN server and client users, PPTP/L2TP
profiles, SNMP: a stored secret shows as a placeholder and is kept on Save);
the Security Review's bulk accept (ack_many: one fold, one audit record, all or
nothing, 100 items / 16 KB); the store rows; the refused-upload report.
httpd.c: apply.cgi and the apply pages refuse action_mode=apply on a GET; a
header-less browser request on the plain-HTTP listener counts as cross-site;
a stock page that no longer ships answers with its bounce stub before the 404.
reaper_inject.c: one table (reaper_pagemap[]) for superseded and removed pages,
the native-page list, the shell framing only .asp pages (a query for Reaper
pages alone), the AiMesh feedback link bounced to Diagnostics. data_arrays.c:
UPnP descriptions JS-escaped (a client's "</script>" no longer ends the
element). sysinfo.c / web-broadcom-am.c: review 2026-10-24 items and the native pages' readbacks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
